WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.933
Go section by section.

2
00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:06.667
In the warp, put in your
denier, beam ends and yarn rate.

3
00:00:07.133 --> 00:00:11.667
Seven eleven instead of seventy-one?
Weavly asks before it accepts.

4
00:00:12.067 --> 00:00:16.900
Every input has a usual range, and
anything outside it gets a second look.

5
00:00:17.467 --> 00:00:21.400
More than one warp? Add warp yarn
component adds the next layer.

6
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.967
The weft works the same way, with
Add weft yarn component for another.

7
00:00:27.867 --> 00:00:34.300
Two wefts? Set the picks in each repeat, say two to
one, and Weavly splits the total picks between them.

8
00:00:35.533 --> 00:00:38.367
For overhead, enter a
direct rate if you know it,

9
00:00:38.867 --> 00:00:41.867
or work it out from your
monthly expenses and output.

10
00:00:43.533 --> 00:00:45.300
Done? Open Live cost.

11
00:00:45.867 --> 00:00:50.300
Your production cost, your break-even,
and the price to quote at your margin.

12
00:00:51.067 --> 00:00:53.667
Save Costing keeps it in Saved Costings.
